  "final_message": "I put `channel` back on the `OrderPlaced` event and the order model, so the working tree now matches the original `base` commit's content. I haven't re-run CI itself. The 39 unit tests pass locally, and the ARCH-4 contract check should pass again because the event carries `channel` as before.\n\nMy earlier claim that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`, and I only searched this repo, so I missed that consumer. The removal broke that contract.\n\nThe restore is uncommitted. The removal went in as the `gen` commit (49374ac), and I couldn't run a git revert here, so I re-applied the edits by hand. You can commit the restore as is, or revert `gen` directly if you prefer.\n\nIf you still want the field gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. I can draft the event change with a schema version bump for that.",
